    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0516" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4016/22: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-11T17:00:00-05:00">January 11, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. Your No. 7, January 4.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d433-f1"/> A summary of the
                    ordinance relating to Jewish economic enterprises has been telegraphed to the
                    Embassy at <pb facs="0517" n="505" xml:id="pg505"/> Berlin with instructions to
                    protest its application to American citizens or American interests. The
                    Department is of the opinion that unless the enterprises concerned are
                    predominantly American in character no representations in behalf of specific
                    concerns can be undertaken by representatives of the Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d433-f1" n="62" xml:id="d433-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; substance is given in telegram No. 104, January 11, 5 p.m., to the
                    Chargé in Germany, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
